I understand completely. We will revert the big stepper back to a beautiful **horizontal** layout.
Regarding the role names (showing 9001 instead of the name): If the Java database JOIN isn't mapping the names correctly yet, the easiest and most bulletproof way to fix this immediately is to map the IDs to their names directly in the frontend.
Here is the updated code. It gives you the **Horizontal Stepper**, adds a **Role Name Mapper**, and places the **Total Time Elapsed** clearly at the top.
### Step 1: Add the Role Mapper Function
Put this right next to your calculateTimeElapsed function (near the top of your component):
```javascript
  const getRoleDisplayName = (roleValue) => {
    // If the backend sends raw IDs, map them to professional names
    const roleMap = {
      "9001": "TCSGLIF Maker/Checker",
      "9002": "SBIGLIF Checker",
      "9003": "Branch Maker",
      "null": "System Execution",
      "System": "System Execution"
    };
    return roleMap[String(roleValue)] || roleValue || "System";
  };

```
